s://github.com/HarshavardhanK/Collatz-Conjecture","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":"The conjecture can be summarized as follows. Take any positive integer n. If n is even, divide it by 2 to get n / 2. If n is odd, multiply it by 3 and add 1 to obtain 3n + 1. Repeat the process (which has been called \"Half Or Triple Plus One\", or HOTPO) indefinitely. The conjecture is that no matter what number you start with, you will always eventually reach 1.","topics":["cpp14","mathematics","numbertheory"],"score":193936,"global_rank":335890},{"name":"cse481sp17/team3","owner":"cse481sp17","html_url":"https://github.com/cse481sp17/team3","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":null,"topics":[],"score":193936,"global_rank":335913},{"name":"margretsteele/cppcon","owner":"margretsteele","html_url":"https://github.com/margretsteele/cppcon","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":"Notes from CPPCON 2016","topics":[],"score":193928,"global_rank":335958},{"name":"cdacamar/tiny_benchmark","owner":"cdacamar","html_url":"https://github.com/cdacamar/tiny_benchmark","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":"YA benchmarking lib","topics":["benchmarking","cpp"],"score":193920,"global_rank":335977},{"name":"annanay25/polly-precompiled","owner":"annanay25","html_url":"https://github.com/annanay25/polly-precompiled","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":"Precompiled Polly libraries for a temporary port to Bazel","topics":[],"score":193920,"global_rank":335996},{"name":"dhasuda/Genetic-algorithm---Sudoku-aula-otimiza-o","owner":"dhasuda","html_url":"https://github.com/dhasuda/Genetic-algorithm---Sudoku-aula-otimiza-o","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"C++","description":null,"topics":[],"score":193912,"global_rank":336013},{"name":"joshbullers/WordGame","owner":"joshbullers","html_url":"https:/